OL,3,GNEWSAFraudster's friend helped in #722k
OL,4,ACovid loan scam
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who played a "vital role" in his
OL,7,Ffraudster friend's #722,000 coronavirus
OL,8,Floan scam has been given a suspended
OL,9,Fsentence.
OL,11,FNeil Moore made more than #37,000 by
OL,12,Fallowing his name to be used for
OL,13,Ffictitious companies, set up by serial
OL,14,Fconman Timothy Paul Nellis, to claim
OL,15,Fgovernment loans intended to help
OL,16,Fbusinesses survive the pandemic,
OL,17,FNewcastle Crown Court heard.
OL,19,FMoore, 58, from Newcastle, was jailed
OL,20,Ffor a year suspended for 18 months
OL,21,Fafter admitting transferring criminal
OL,22,Fproperty.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
